  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ndpi_search_kerberos",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/kerberos.c",
    "description": "Heap out-of-bounds read due to missing bounds check before reading `packet->payload[name_offset]` at line ~501 in the AS-REQ parsing path. The code conditionally adjusts `name_offset` (including increments at lines ~488, ~492, ~498) but does not re-validate that `name_offset < packet->payload_packet_len` immediately before dereferencing. This allows `name_offset` to become equal to payload length and causes a 1-byte read past the buffer end.",
    "conditions": "In `fuzz_process_packet`, attacker-controlled `Data/Size` are passed directly to `ndpi_detection_process_packet`, which reaches Kerberos dissector `ndpi_search_kerberos`. A crafted Kerberos-like payload that satisfies earlier ASN.1/msg-type checks and enters the AS-REQ branch can drive `name_offset` updates so it lands at the end of the packet; then `cname_len = packet->payload[name_offset]` reads out of bounds. No additional heap grooming is required; just packet contents/length that pass the parser\u2019s preceding checks."
  },
